# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/herbalism
title Herbalism 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Herbalism 1-300 for both factions: for each skill band, a loop the arrow walks
# through the densest ground of herbs the skill can pick (expected skill-ups per
# yard of a lap, with the time to pick each herb and the herbs' respawn), at
# the lowest character level that keeps the loop nearly as good: no creature on
# it more than a level above that level, and away from the other faction's
# towns. Herbs are the Forever server's own spawns with the chance its spawn
# pools keep each up, and what a herb gives comes from players' recorded
# gathers (tools/lib/professions/gathering/gathering-nodes.json).
# Skill needed per herb: Peacebloom, Silverleaf 1, Earthroot 15, Mageroyal 50,
# Briarthorn 70, Stranglekelp 85, Bruiseweed 100, Wild Steelbloom 115, Grave
# Moss 120, Kingsblood 125, Liferoot 150, Fadeleaf 160, Goldthorn 170,
# Khadgar's Whisker 185, Wintersbite 195, Firebloom 205, Purple Lotus 210,
# Arthas' Tears 220, Sungrass 230, Blindweed 235, Ghost Mushroom 245,
# Gromsblood 250, Golden Sansam 260, Dreamfoil 270, Mountain Silversage 280,
# Plaguebloom 285, Icecap 290, Black Lotus 300.
#
# Herb and ore spawns come from the Forever TrinityCore world DB (its spawn pools
# say how often each is up); beast spawns and levels from the reference data;
# trainer learn skills and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes
# and their skill colours from the Forever client tables.
# Zones are ranked for a character of a fifth of the band's skill in levels (at
# least 5; ASSUMED: one levelling with the profession); a loop that asks more
# says so with a `level` goal, and loses half its worth per level it asks above.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and players' recordings show Expert Mining
# trained at 15 and Artisan Skinning at 29.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Herbalism 1-50

step Learn Herbalism
  tip Any Herbalism trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Herbalism at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Herbalism Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Turn on Find Herbs (spellbook, General tab) so herbs show on the minimap. Forever's starting areas also have Wilted Peacebloom and Stunted Silverleaf (skill 1). The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Wild Harvest as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors sell the Apprentice's Herb Pouch, a four-slot bag for herbs (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Herbalism: hand it in to the herbalism trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Incense Candle recipe.
  train Herbalism Apprentice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Herbalism 1-50

step Stunted Silverleaf & Wilted Peacebloom (1-15)
  tip Walk the loop and pick every Peacebloom (1, orange), Silverleaf (1, orange), Stunted Silverleaf (1, orange), Wilted Peacebloom (1, orange) on the way until Herbalism 15. The Elwynn Forest, Dun Morogh, Tirisfal Glades, Durotar, Teldrassil loops have no Peacebloom, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The Elwynn Forest, Dun Morogh, Tirisfal Glades, Teldrassil loops have no Silverleaf, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The Zephras Isle loop has no Stunted Silverleaf, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The Zephras Isle loop has no Wilted Peacebloom, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 10 herbs for these 14 points: about 5 Peacebloom and 5 Silverleaf. For Alchemy: about 110 Peacebloom and 85 Silverleaf in all.
