step Stranglekelp & Bruiseweed (100-115)
  tip Walk the loop and pick every Peacebloom (1, green, rare), Silverleaf (1, green, rare), Earthroot (15, green, rare), Mageroyal (50, green), Briarthorn (70, yellow), Stranglekelp (85, orange), Bruiseweed (100, orange) on the way until Herbalism 115. Mageroyal and Briarthorn sometimes give a Swiftthistle as well. Stranglekelp grows underwater along the shore: watch your breath. The Loch Modan, Stonetalon Mountains, Redridge Mountains, The Barrens loops have no Stranglekelp, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The Stranglethorn Vale, The Hinterlands loops have no Bruiseweed, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. A quest in these zones needs Herbalism: Root Samples (level 16, Mebok Mizzyrix, The Barrens). The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 20 herbs for these 15 points: about 15 Bruiseweed, 10 Stranglekelp, 5 Briarthorn, 5 Mageroyal and 5 Swiftthistle. For Alchemy: about 60 Bruiseweed, 40 Stranglekelp, 160 Briarthorn and 50 Mageroyal in all.
