# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Herbalism 125-160
section Herbalism 125-160

step Expert Herbalism
  tip Expert Herbalism raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and no character level, and costs 50s: train it as soon as you reach 125. The arrow picks the nearest Herbalism trainer of your faction.
  train Herbalism Expert

step Bruiseweed & Kingsblood (125-150)
  tip Walk the loop and pick every Mageroyal (50, green), Briarthorn (70, green), Bruiseweed (100, yellow), Wild Steelbloom (115, orange), Grave Moss (120, orange, rare), Kingsblood (125, orange) on the way until Herbalism 150. Mageroyal and Briarthorn sometimes give a Swiftthistle as well. Grave Moss grows in graveyards and crypts. The Loch Modan, The Barrens, Riverglades loops have no Wild Steelbloom, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. The Loch Modan loop has no Kingsblood, so fewer points a lap: worth it only when the zone suits your level better. A quest in these zones needs Herbalism: Root Samples (level 16, Mebok Mizzyrix, The Barrens). The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 40 herbs for these 25 points: about 25 Kingsblood, 25 Bruiseweed, 10 Wild Steelbloom, 10 Briarthorn, 5 Mageroyal, 5 Swiftthistle, 5 Grave Moss and 5 Frilled Lichen. For Alchemy: about 40 Kingsblood, 60 Bruiseweed, 45 Wild Steelbloom, 160 Briarthorn and 50 Mageroyal in all.
